      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:fo7fzo'
    '|a||It fell, and not by a little.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||It fell. A German forester later put the loss over two or three generations of pure spruce at 20 to 30 percent.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||From the best foresters in the world? What went wrong?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:9btf9b'
    '|a||Tidiness, partly. They cleared the underbrush, the fallen wood and the dead standing trees, and with them the insects, birds and fungi that build the soil.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:swc7dj'
    '|a||Nobody stole anything. How a forest feeds itself simply wasn''t in their tables, and ecologists still don''t fully understand it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:mhnnbx'
    '|b||So that''s the puzzle: a failure with no villain in it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:2kmi4e'
    '|a||To see how, ask any official two separate questions: does she want what the public wants, and does she know enough to get it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||If she doesn''t want it, because of a bribe, a vote to win or a career to protect, that''s an incentive failure.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:w01quw'
    '|a||If she wants it but can''t know enough, that''s a knowledge failure. The foresters sit right here.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:10cp9bt'
    '|b||Your turn. Sort these four into the two kinds of failure.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1iyj5mw'
    '|b||Which failed for want of will, and which for want of knowledge? Sort each case.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:171yygm'
    '|a||The test: would she have done better by wanting harder, or by knowing more?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5640
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Then try this on the foresters: pay each of them a bonus for every cubic metre of wood. Does the forest come back?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:zwcm58'
    '|a||No. A bonus fixes wanting, not knowing. They''d plant the same rows of spruce, only faster.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1llm37h'
    '|a||Knowledge goes missing in four ways. It can be dispersed: Hayek''s point that what an economy runs on is scattered in scraps across millions of heads.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ywyg1g'
    '|b||It can be tacit: known but never written down, like a fisher''s feel for when the weather will turn.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1glksm5'
    '|a||It can be changing: true when the plan was written, stale by the time it''s carried out.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:11y2quq'
    '|b||Or it can be unknowable: nobody knows it yet, not even the experts. The forest soil was that.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:2j9zh2'
    '|a||So the two failures need different cures: watchdogs and bonuses fix wanting; only finding out fixes knowing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:4zls5b'
    '|a||The hardest kind is the knowledge nobody has. Here''s a case of it, from Bangladesh.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5760
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Pond and river water there spread cholera and diarrhoea, which killed many children.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:148txni'
    '|a||So from the 1970s the government, backed by UNICEF and the World Bank, pushed millions of tube wells: groundwater pumped up a pipe, free of germs.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:fjr2r6'
    '|b||But nobody tested that water for arsenic, a poison that seeps naturally from the sediments underground.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ra17y2'
    '|a||In the early 1990s, arsenic turned up in the wells, across huge parts of the country.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:3yypjl'
    '|b||A paper in the WHO''s Bulletin in 2000 called it the largest poisoning of a population in history: 35 to 77 million people at risk, out of 125 million.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:nwqy8o'
    '|a||Well-meant, done competently, and wrong about something nobody knew to ask. So what helped?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:12datwl'
    '|a||Not a smarter plan from the capital. Testers went from well to well and painted each spout: green for safe, red for unsafe.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:8cfwqk'
    '|b||Guess first: when a family learned their own well was red, how much more likely were they to switch within a year?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:19mafgm'
    '|b||Click on the line where you think it is.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1u3mm6d'
    '|a||Thirty-seven percentage points more likely, in one large study. Many simply walked to a neighbour''s green well.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||So a red spout works a bit like a price: one cheap signal, put right where the decision is made.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1im6snu'
    '|a||That''s the cure for a knowledge failure: find out, and get what you found to the people who choose.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:skgcg1'
    '|b||But was this really a government failure? Most of those wells weren''t the state''s.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Fair point. In one district surveyed in 2000, 94 percent of the wells were privately owned, put in by small local firms.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1xmv1jm'
    '|b||So families and the market didn''t know about the arsenic either. The unknowable is unknowable for everyone.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1u9a9gq'
    '|a||True. The difference is scale and feedback: a plan copies one mistake everywhere at once, like the same spruce across a country''s forests.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1nh8cr2'
    '|b||And it was the state that tested the wells and painted the spouts. Governments find things out too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:zdijft'
    '|a||And the two failures tangle: a mistake lasts longer when nobody has a reason to go looking for it.':
